{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K3yhhDSmQYZALhXDjnRNeu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/projects/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\", \"D4 Community and Collaboration\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"sandbox\", \"incubating\", \"graduated\", \"graduated-projects\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# CNCF Projects — maturity levels (cncf.io/projects/)\n9\t\n10\t- **Graduated** — projects considered stable, widely adopted, and production ready, attracting thousands of contributors.\n11\t- **Incubating** — projects used successfully in production by a small number of users with a healthy pool of contributors.\n12\t- **Sandbox** — experimental projects not yet widely tested in production, on the bleeding edge of technology.\n13\t\n14\tGraduated projects listed on the page (2026-08-23): Argo, Buildpacks, cert-manager, Cilium, CloudEvents, containerd, CoreDNS, CRI-O, Crossplane, CubeFS, Dapr, Dragonfly, Envoy, etcd, Falco, Fluentd, Flux, Harbor, Helm, in-toto, Istio, Jaeger, KEDA, Knative, KubeEdge, Kubeflow, Kubernetes, Kyverno, Linkerd, Open Policy Agent (OPA), OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Rook, SPIFFE, SPIRE, The Update Framework (TUF), TiKV, Vitess.\n15\t\n16\tNote: graduation criteria (due diligence, adopters, governance, security audit, etc.) are defined in the CNCF TOC's project lifecycle documentation (github.com/cncf/toc), not on this page.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"7da540b8-9123-4c3e-bb1b-e784cbe8cbe4","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:34:04.923Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\cncf-project-maturity-levels-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/projects/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\", \"D4 Community and Collaboration\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"sandbox\", \"incubating\", \"graduated\", \"graduated-projects\"]\n---\n# CNCF Projects — maturity levels (cncf.io/projects/)\n\n- **Graduated** — projects considered stable, widely adopted, and production ready, attracting thousands of contributors.\n- **Incubating** — projects used successfully in production by a small number of users with a healthy pool of contributors.\n- **Sandbox** — experimental projects not yet widely tested in production, on the bleeding edge of technology.\n\nGraduated projects listed on the page (2026-08-23): Argo, Buildpacks, cert-manager, Cilium, CloudEvents, containerd, CoreDNS, CRI-O, Crossplane, CubeFS, Dapr, Dragonfly, Envoy, etcd, Falco, Fluentd, Flux, Harbor, Helm, in-toto, Istio, Jaeger, KEDA, Knative, KubeEdge, Kubeflow, Kubernetes, Kyverno, Linkerd, Open Policy Agent (OPA), OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Rook, SPIFFE, SPIRE, The Update Framework (TUF), TiKV, Vitess.\n\nNote: graduation criteria (due diligence, adopters, governance, security audit, etc.) are defined in the CNCF TOC's project lifecycle documentation (github.com/cncf/toc), not on this page.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}}}
