{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sqdj6pTdF3gT2KiWRyzFK5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/toc/blob/main/README.md\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:45:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation Technical Oversight Committee\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Community and Collaboration\", \"D4 Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"toc\", \"tags\", \"technical-advisory-groups\", \"governing-board\", \"project-lifecycle\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# CNCF Technical Oversight Committee (github.com/cncf/toc)\n9\t\n10\tThe CNCF TOC is the technical governing body of the CNCF. Its responsibilities include: defining and maintaining the technical vision and principles for the Cloud Native Computing Foundation; approving new projects within the scope of the CNCF set by the Governing Board; creating a conceptual architecture for the projects, aligning projects, removing or archiving projects; accepting feedback from the end user technical advisory board and mapping it to projects; aligning interfaces to components under management and establishing common practices across projects.\n11\t\n12\t## Technical Advisory Groups (TAGs) — active as of this snapshot\n13\tTAG Developer Experience; TAG Infrastructure; TAG Operational Resilience; TAG Security and Compliance; TAG Workloads Foundation. (The TAGs were restructured in 2025 from the earlier set: App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage.)\n14\t\n15\t## Project maturity\n16\tProjects enter the CNCF at the Sandbox level and may progress to Incubating and Graduated as they meet the criteria in the project lifecycle documentation (adoption, governance, security practices, contributor diversity). The CNCF provides services to projects at each level, with the broadest support for incubating and graduated projects.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"c00e2491-432c-4820-8527-085e2e14a257","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:34:05.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\cncf-toc-and-tags-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/toc/blob/main/README.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:45:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation Technical Oversight Committee\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Community and Collaboration\", \"D4 Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"toc\", \"tags\", \"technical-advisory-groups\", \"governing-board\", \"project-lifecycle\"]\n---\n# CNCF Technical Oversight Committee (github.com/cncf/toc)\n\nThe CNCF TOC is the technical governing body of the CNCF. Its responsibilities include: defining and maintaining the technical vision and principles for the Cloud Native Computing Foundation; approving new projects within the scope of the CNCF set by the Governing Board; creating a conceptual architecture for the projects, aligning projects, removing or archiving projects; accepting feedback from the end user technical advisory board and mapping it to projects; aligning interfaces to components under management and establishing common practices across projects.\n\n## Technical Advisory Groups (TAGs) — active as of this snapshot\nTAG Developer Experience; TAG Infrastructure; TAG Operational Resilience; TAG Security and Compliance; TAG Workloads Foundation. (The TAGs were restructured in 2025 from the earlier set: App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage.)\n\n## Project maturity\nProjects enter the CNCF at the Sandbox level and may progress to Incubating and Graduated as they meet the criteria in the project lifecycle documentation (adoption, governance, security practices, contributor diversity). The CNCF provides services to projects at each level, with the broadest support for incubating and graduated projects.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}}}
