{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016m9V2EfTWXZLbNa6GRF1Ys","type":"tool_result","content":"# KEDA: Key Definitions from Official Documentation\n\n**What KEDA Is:**\n\"KEDA is a tool that helps Kubernetes scale applications based on real-world events. It was created by Microsoft and Red Hat.\"\n\n**What It Does:**\n\"With KEDA, you can adjust the size of your containers automatically, depending on the workload—like the number of messages in a queue or incoming requests.\"\n\n**How It Works with Horizontal Pod Autoscaler:**\n\"It's lightweight and works alongside Kubernetes components like the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA). It doesn't replace anything but adds more functionality.\"\n\n**What a Scaler Is:**\n\"Scalers connect to event sources like message queues or databases, pulling data on current usage or load.\"\n\n**Scale-to-Zero:**\nThe documentation does not mention scale-to-zero capabilities.\n\n**CNCF Affiliation:**\nThe documentation does not reference CNCF affiliation or graduation status. It notes KEDA was \"created by Microsoft and Red Hat\" and references \"The Linux Foundation\" in the footer regarding trademarks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"5d51530d-e8cb-44fe-a0ec-dc7f39bd64a0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:35:54.000Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":39303,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# KEDA: Key Definitions from Official Documentation\n\n**What KEDA Is:**\n\"KEDA is a tool that helps Kubernetes scale applications based on real-world events. It was created by Microsoft and Red Hat.\"\n\n**What It Does:**\n\"With KEDA, you can adjust the size of your containers automatically, depending on the workload—like the number of messages in a queue or incoming requests.\"\n\n**How It Works with Horizontal Pod Autoscaler:**\n\"It's lightweight and works alongside Kubernetes components like the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA). It doesn't replace anything but adds more functionality.\"\n\n**What a Scaler Is:**\n\"Scalers connect to event sources like message queues or databases, pulling data on current usage or load.\"\n\n**Scale-to-Zero:**\nThe documentation does not mention scale-to-zero capabilities.\n\n**CNCF Affiliation:**\nThe documentation does not reference CNCF affiliation or graduation status. It notes KEDA was \"created by Microsoft and Red Hat\" and references \"The Linux Foundation\" in the footer regarding trademarks.","durationMs":4398,"url":"https://keda.sh/docs/2.17/concepts/"}}
