{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LG3cgL4sDGC3WVTMGZiWMJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CNCF Project Lifecycle Levels\n\nThe four maturity stages are: **\"Sandbox - Experimental or innovative projects early in their development,\"** **\"Incubation - Projects gaining adoption, focusing on improving stability and maturity,\"** **\"Graduated - Highly mature, robust projects whose adopters have demonstrated their production-readiness,\"** and **\"Archived - Inactive or low activity projects that are no longer supported.\"**\n\n## Movement Process\n\nTo advance levels, projects must **\"submit an incubation or graduation application issue on the TOC repo\"** and provide evidence of meeting criteria. They must also **\"complete the Adopter Interview Form with 5-7 adopters willing to be interviewed\"** and provide self-assessed technical and governance reviews.\n\n## Due Diligence Requirements\n\nA TOC sponsor is assigned to conduct evaluation. The sponsor holds **\"an Application Kick off Meeting\"** with the project, then performs **\"Due Diligence creation or refresh\"** where they craft a PR evaluating the project's completion of criteria. **\"Adopter Interviews are conducted\"** by TOC sponsors, followed by **\"a TOC internal comment period, about 1 week, for other TOC members.\"**\n\n## Voting & Decision\n\n**\"The public comment period is open for two weeks.\"** After that, **\"the TOC opens voting on the PR using gitvote.\"** The result: **\"If the vote passes (2/3 supermajority vote of the TOC), the results are emailed.\"**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"124cfd69-65a5-4012-a1d2-ec575b93551a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:37:13.505Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":366860,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CNCF Project Lifecycle Levels\n\nThe four maturity stages are: **\"Sandbox - Experimental or innovative projects early in their development,\"** **\"Incubation - Projects gaining adoption, focusing on improving stability and maturity,\"** **\"Graduated - Highly mature, robust projects whose adopters have demonstrated their production-readiness,\"** and **\"Archived - Inactive or low activity projects that are no longer supported.\"**\n\n## Movement Process\n\nTo advance levels, projects must **\"submit an incubation or graduation application issue on the TOC repo\"** and provide evidence of meeting criteria. They must also **\"complete the Adopter Interview Form with 5-7 adopters willing to be interviewed\"** and provide self-assessed technical and governance reviews.\n\n## Due Diligence Requirements\n\nA TOC sponsor is assigned to conduct evaluation. The sponsor holds **\"an Application Kick off Meeting\"** with the project, then performs **\"Due Diligence creation or refresh\"** where they craft a PR evaluating the project's completion of criteria. **\"Adopter Interviews are conducted\"** by TOC sponsors, followed by **\"a TOC internal comment period, about 1 week, for other TOC members.\"**\n\n## Voting & Decision\n\n**\"The public comment period is open for two weeks.\"** After that, **\"the TOC opens voting on the PR using gitvote.\"** The result: **\"If the vote passes (2/3 supermajority vote of the TOC), the results are emailed.\"**","durationMs":6382,"url":"https://github.com/cncf/toc/blob/main/process/README.md"}}
