{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RGLqxVgoyzhaarnvRWmKcL","type":"tool_result","content":"# CNCF Charter - Key Statements\n\n**CNCF Mission:**\n\"The Foundation's mission is to make cloud native computing ubiquitous.\"\n\n**Governing Board Responsibilities:**\n\"The CNCF Governing Board will be responsible for marketing and other business oversight and budget decisions for the CNCF.\"\n\n**Technical Oversight Committee Responsibilities:**\n\"The TOC is expected to facilitate driving neutral consensus for: defining and maintaining the technical vision for the Cloud Native Computing Foundation...\"\n\n**End User Technical Advisory Board Role:**\n\"The End User TAB will serve as the voice of End Users in the CNCF community, advance topics of concern to End Users, and raise awareness about the needs and perspectives of end users.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"318283aa-cadf-4132-a4c5-37008f54e8a2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:37:48.425Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":404065,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CNCF Charter - Key Statements\n\n**CNCF Mission:**\n\"The Foundation's mission is to make cloud native computing ubiquitous.\"\n\n**Governing Board Responsibilities:**\n\"The CNCF Governing Board will be responsible for marketing and other business oversight and budget decisions for the CNCF.\"\n\n**Technical Oversight Committee Responsibilities:**\n\"The TOC is expected to facilitate driving neutral consensus for: defining and maintaining the technical vision for the Cloud Native Computing Foundation...\"\n\n**End User Technical Advisory Board Role:**\n\"The End User TAB will serve as the voice of End Users in the CNCF community, advance topics of concern to End Users, and raise awareness about the needs and perspectives of end users.\"","durationMs":3433,"url":"https://github.com/cncf/foundation/blob/main/charter.md"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZS8vdQ9AvyKiz9dP5aGh2","type":"tool_result","content":"# KEDA: Key Definitions from Documentation\n\n**What KEDA is:**\n\"KEDA is a tool that helps Kubernetes scale applications based on real-world events.\"\n\n**Lightweight component note:**\nThe documentation does not contain the exact phrase about KEDA being a \"single-purpose lightweight component that can be added to any Kubernetes cluster.\" However, it does state: \"It's lightweight and works alongside Kubernetes components like the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA).\"\n\n**Relationship with HPA:**\n\"It doesn't replace anything but adds more functionality\" and works \"in conjunction with the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler.\"\n\n**What scalers are:**\n\"Scalers connect to event sources like message queues or databases, pulling data on current usage or load.\"\n\n**Scaling from zero to N:**\nThe documentation does not explicitly mention \"scaling from zero to N\" in these exact terms."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"ada10d37-547d-43ab-b79b-d1b3306879a1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:37:50.073Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":41536,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# KEDA: Key Definitions from Documentation\n\n**What KEDA is:**\n\"KEDA is a tool that helps Kubernetes scale applications based on real-world events.\"\n\n**Lightweight component note:**\nThe documentation does not contain the exact phrase about KEDA being a \"single-purpose lightweight component that can be added to any Kubernetes cluster.\" However, it does state: \"It's lightweight and works alongside Kubernetes components like the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA).\"\n\n**Relationship with HPA:**\n\"It doesn't replace anything but adds more functionality\" and works \"in conjunction with the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler.\"\n\n**What scalers are:**\n\"Scalers connect to event sources like message queues or databases, pulling data on current usage or load.\"\n\n**Scaling from zero to N:**\nThe documentation does not explicitly mention \"scaling from zero to N\" in these exact terms.","durationMs":3680,"url":"https://keda.sh/docs/2.18/concepts/"}}
