{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013qHNQW2VddsXZYyWtPfK2s","type":"tool_result","content":"# Kubernetes Release Information\n\nHere are the exact quotes from the page:\n\n**Release branches maintained:**\n\"The Kubernetes project maintains release branches for the most recent three minor releases (1.37, 1.36, 1.35).\"\n\n**Patch support duration:**\n\"Kubernetes 1.19 and newer receive approximately 1 year of patch support. Kubernetes 1.18 and older received approximately 9 months of patch support.\"\n\n**Currently supported releases with end-of-life dates:**\n\n1. Version 1.37 - \"End of Life: 2027-10-28\"\n2. Version 1.36 - \"End of Life: 2027-06-28\"\n3. Version 1.35 - \"End of Life: 2027-02-28\"\n\n**Release cadence statement:**\nThe page does not contain any explicit statement about release cadence (how many minor releases per year or how many weeks per cycle). That information is not included in the provided content."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"8c245aaa-4435-4e4e-9c8f-a856fb5f6e2e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:38:50.573Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":54952,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Kubernetes Release Information\n\nHere are the exact quotes from the page:\n\n**Release branches maintained:**\n\"The Kubernetes project maintains release branches for the most recent three minor releases (1.37, 1.36, 1.35).\"\n\n**Patch support duration:**\n\"Kubernetes 1.19 and newer receive approximately 1 year of patch support. Kubernetes 1.18 and older received approximately 9 months of patch support.\"\n\n**Currently supported releases with end-of-life dates:**\n\n1. Version 1.37 - \"End of Life: 2027-10-28\"\n2. Version 1.36 - \"End of Life: 2027-06-28\"\n3. Version 1.35 - \"End of Life: 2027-02-28\"\n\n**Release cadence statement:**\nThe page does not contain any explicit statement about release cadence (how many minor releases per year or how many weeks per cycle). That information is not included in the provided content.","durationMs":3117,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/releases/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KiU4oEc9jmw8ZNt4X4fKKR","type":"tool_result","content":"# CNCF Guidance for New Contributors\n\n## Getting Started\n\n\"Are you new to open source? If so, we recommend checking out our comprehensive guide, 'Start Contributing to Open Source'.\"\n\nThe guide covers \"communities and projects, how to find them, how to conform to community standards.\"\n\n## Mentorship Programs\n\n**LFX Mentorship:** Described as a \"mentoring initiative by the Linux Foundation\"\n\n**Google Summer of Code:** Characterized as a \"mentoring program for the open source beginners\"\n\n**Outreachy:** Identified as a \"mentoring initiative for the communities traditionally underrepresented in tech\"\n\n## Community Groups\n\n\"The Cloud Native Computing Foundation supports the worldwide community of the Cloud Native Community Groups (CNCGs).\" They're listed on community.cncf.io.\n\nThe CNCF also encourages new local communities, stating: \"CNCF is currently working on expanding the Cloud Native community worldwide.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"95c230d7-0bd4-4c63-8b08-e2b8d19c5b52","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:38:52.308Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":26280,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CNCF Guidance for New Contributors\n\n## Getting Started\n\n\"Are you new to open source? If so, we recommend checking out our comprehensive guide, 'Start Contributing to Open Source'.\"\n\nThe guide covers \"communities and projects, how to find them, how to conform to community standards.\"\n\n## Mentorship Programs\n\n**LFX Mentorship:** Described as a \"mentoring initiative by the Linux Foundation\"\n\n**Google Summer of Code:** Characterized as a \"mentoring program for the open source beginners\"\n\n**Outreachy:** Identified as a \"mentoring initiative for the communities traditionally underrepresented in tech\"\n\n## Community Groups\n\n\"The Cloud Native Computing Foundation supports the worldwide community of the Cloud Native Community Groups (CNCGs).\" They're listed on community.cncf.io.\n\nThe CNCF also encourages new local communities, stating: \"CNCF is currently working on expanding the Cloud Native community worldwide.\"","durationMs":3388,"url":"https://contribute.cncf.io/contributors/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DahUGL4w5XUsij2JtVBsLn","type":"tool_result","content":"# Vertical Pod Autoscaling - Key Information\n\n## What is VerticalPodAutoscaler\n\n\"In Kubernetes, a _VerticalPodAutoscaler_ automatically updates a workload management [resource](/docs/reference/using-api/api-concepts/#standard-api-terminology \"A Kubernetes entity, representing an endpoint on the Kubernetes API server.\") (such as a [Deployment](/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/deployment/ \"Manages a replicated application on your cluster.\") or [StatefulSet](/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/statefulset/ \"A StatefulSet manages deployment and scaling of a set of Pods, with durable storage and persistent identifiers for each Pod.\")), with the aim of automatically adjusting infrastructure [resource](/docs/reference/glossary/?all=true#term-infrastructure-resource \"A defined amount of infrastructure available for consumption (CPU, memory, etc).\") [requests and limits](/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/#requests-and-limits) to match actual usage.\"\n\n## Installation Note\n\n\"Unlike HorizontalPodAutoscaler, which is part of the core Kubernetes API, VPA must be installed separately in your cluster.\"\n\n## Main Components\n\n\"The VPA consists of three main components:\n\n*   The _recommender_, which analyzes resource usage and provides recommendations.\n*   The _updater_, that Pod resource requests either by evicting Pods or modifying them in place.\n*   And the VPA _admission controller_ webhook, which applies resource recommendations to new or recreated Pods.\"\n\n## Update Modes Supported\n\n- **Off**\n- **Initial**\n- **Recreate**\n- **InPlaceOrRecreate**\n- **InPlace**\n- **Auto (deprecated)**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","uuid":"e5daa1ba-9969-4bb7-ab1a-6b0e2bd863e8","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:38:56.603Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":518787,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Vertical Pod Autoscaling - Key Information\n\n## What is VerticalPodAutoscaler\n\n\"In Kubernetes, a _VerticalPodAutoscaler_ automatically updates a workload management [resource](/docs/reference/using-api/api-concepts/#standard-api-terminology \"A Kubernetes entity, representing an endpoint on the Kubernetes API server.\") (such as a [Deployment](/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/deployment/ \"Manages a replicated application on your cluster.\") or [StatefulSet](/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/statefulset/ \"A StatefulSet manages deployment and scaling of a set of Pods, with durable storage and persistent identifiers for each Pod.\")), with the aim of automatically adjusting infrastructure [resource](/docs/reference/glossary/?all=true#term-infrastructure-resource \"A defined amount of infrastructure available for consumption (CPU, memory, etc).\") [requests and limits](/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/#requests-and-limits) to match actual usage.\"\n\n## Installation Note\n\n\"Unlike HorizontalPodAutoscaler, which is part of the core Kubernetes API, VPA must be installed separately in your cluster.\"\n\n## Main Components\n\n\"The VPA consists of three main components:\n\n*   The _recommender_, which analyzes resource usage and provides recommendations.\n*   The _updater_, that Pod resource requests either by evicting Pods or modifying them in place.\n*   And the VPA _admission controller_ webhook, which applies resource recommendations to new or recreated Pods.\"\n\n## Update Modes Supported\n\n- **Off**\n- **Initial**\n- **Recreate**\n- **InPlaceOrRecreate**\n- **InPlace**\n- **Auto (deprecated)**","durationMs":6287,"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/autoscaling/vertical-pod-autoscale/"}}
