{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" glossary entries, fetched together because §3 teaches them as a\nmutually reinforcing set rather than as separate definitions.\n\n## Microservices Architecture ("}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"6719a213-f4e1-4e3c-8ad0-2152ec431f5a"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"glossary.cncf.io/microservices-architecture/)\n\nDefinition, verbatim:\n\n> \"A microservices architecture is an architectural approach that breaks\n> applications into individual independent (micro)services, with each service\n> focused on a specific funct"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"9f0ee4bb-a9f7-4ab2-9343-1b4eec024f3a"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ionality.\"\n\nProblem it addresses — verbatim fragment:\n\n> \"the entire app would have to be scaled to accommodate the increase — a very\n> inefficient use of resources\"\n\n[Paraphrase of"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"863fae5c-b60f-40a3-8627-a8fd5d6961af"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" surrounding text, NOT verbatim: the entry states that the\ntraditional monolithic approach creates inefficiencies; that monoliths encourage\ntight coupling and make"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"97c18e9f-84a1-4716-a5b9-72b3bddc178d"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" it harder to enforce separation of concerns; and that\nthey require developers to understand the entire codebase before making changes.]\n\nHow it helps — verbatim fragments:\n\n> \"different teams to work simultaneously on a small part of a bigger application\n> without in"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"b333db37-f487-443c-a837-aa8271db1aca"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"advertently negatively impacting the rest of the app\"\n\n> \"it also creates operational overhead — the things you need to deploy and keep\n> track of increase by order of magnitude\"\n\n[Paraphrase, NOT verbatim:"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"63d5288b-e61d-4dac-b544-a0217113e7c2"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" breaking functionality into separate services enables\nindependent deployment, updates, and scaling; the entry notes that many\ncloud native technologies have emerged to address the operational challenges\ninherent in microservices deployments.]\n\n## Monolithic Apps (glossary.c"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"12cbb69c-e93e-4a8c-86fb-7afb370cb5bb"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ncf.io/monolithic-apps/) — verbatim, complete\n\nA monolithic application contains all functionality in a single deployable\nprogram. This is often the simplest and easiest place to start when making an\napplication. However"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"5c791673-99b5-41fe-a946-66249cf38347"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", once the application grows in complexity, monoliths can\nbecome hard to maintain. With more developers working on the same codebase, the\nlikelihood of conflicting changes and the need for interpersonal communication\nbetween developers increases.\n\n**Problem it"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"45b55374-974f-48bf-9215-af66f179f273"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Addresses**\n\nDevolving an application into microservices increases its operational overhead —\nthere are more things to test, deploy, and keep running. Early in a product's\nlifecycle, it may be advantageous to def"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"8f477d00-c265-4651-b590-c10cd3c9bc20"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"er this complexity and build a monolithic\napplication until the product is determined successful.\n\n**How it Helps**\n\nA well-designed monolith can uphold lean principles by being the simplest way to\nget an application up and running. When the business"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"e94be68f-f2b3-40c3-9e18-a1880a91af4e"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" value of the monolithic\napplication proves successful, it can be decomposed into microservices. Crafting\na microservices-based app before it has proven valuable may be premature spending\nof engineering effort."}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"4aaacef2-b161-43be-96d9-f89cc398ee50"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" If the application yields no value, that effort becomes\nwasted.\n\n## Loosely Coupled Architecture (glossary.cncf.io/loosely-coupled-architecture/) — verbatim, complete\n\nLoosely coupled architecture is an architectural style where the individual\ncomponents of an application are"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"035161db-25a6-409b-bb67-0048f7a6c65d"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" built independently from one another (the\nopposite paradigm of tightly coupled architectures). Each component, sometimes\nreferred to as a microservice, is built to perform a specific function in a way\nthat can be used by any number of other services. This p"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"ad161fc6-5e31-4aa9-a552-1bdcc1cf4615"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"attern is generally\nslower to implement than tightly coupled architecture but has a number of\nbenefits, particularly as applications scale.\n\nLoosely coupled applications allow teams to develop features, deploy, and scale\nindependently, which all"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"be4dd3be-2953-4faf-a547-22d7b66d6594"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ows organizations to iterate quickly on individual\ncomponents. Application development is faster and teams can be structured around\ntheir competency, focusing on their specific application.\n```\n\n### A2 · `cncf-glossary-immutable-infrastructure-2"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"0d62e10a-2574-4fc0-950c-3b7cc84f05be"}
