{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" CNCF says \"without requiring code\nchanges\"; Istio says \"without code changes\".\n\n## Service Mesh\n\nIn a microservices world, apps are broken down into multiple smaller services\nthat communicate over a network. Just like your"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"700d4ddd-6a71-4a9a-a55c-2bbffbaee7a1"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" wifi network, computer networks\nare intrinsically unreliable, hackable, and often slow. Service meshes address\nthis new set of challenges by managing traffic (i.e., communication) between"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"503f93ab-1d97-476e-9e20-ad4bd1549b8b"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\nservices and adding reliability, observability, and security features uniformly\nacross all services.\n\n## Problem it addresses\n\nHaving moved to a microservices architecture, engineers are now dealing with\nhundreds, possibly even thousands of individual services, all needing to"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"b94e6b8f-54a8-4bc2-8449-7c0b0d4f6ed8"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\ncommunicate. That means a lot of traffic is going back and forth over the\nnetwork. On top of that, individual applications may need to encrypt\ncommunications to support regulatory requirements, provide common metrics to\noperations teams, or provide det"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"fec8dd90-56d5-4704-a8c6-007342e83a55"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ailed insight into traffic to help diagnose\nissues. If built into the individual applications, each one of these features\nwill cause friction between teams and slow down development of new features.\n\n## How it helps\n\nService meshes add reliability, observability, and security"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"b974037c-d578-4ae9-8de0-d320d954b376"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" features uniformly\nacross all services across a cluster without requiring code changes. Before\nservice meshes, that functionality had to be encoded into every single service,\nbecoming a potential source of bugs and technical debt.\n\nThe Sidecar Container model"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"735780eb-e58f-492d-aef9-c3b2b250cd98"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" pairs each pod with a proxy. This per-pod proxy\nintercepts and manages network traffic, enforces security policies, balances\nworkloads, and collects performance data for each service. While this approach\noffers excellent control and service-specific traffic management, it also uses\nmore comput"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"eb34412a-877d-4cb4-aea4-840e148491f1"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ing resources and becomes more complex to manage as your system grows.\n\nA Sidecarless design, on the other hand, moves the aforementioned mesh\nfunctionality to the operating system level by using kernel features like"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"36b2f438-c2ac-49c7-ad87-f64d5d01c3fc"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" eBPF.\nBy doing away with per-pod proxies, this method drastically reduces resource\nusage and removes unnecessary network hops, which lowers latency and boosts\nperformance. Because overhead remains constant regardless of pod count and"}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"7138e503-d572-4671-b89d-0742032d1f33"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" there\nare fewer agents to deploy, teams benefit from simplified operations and linear\nscalability as workload increases.\n\n---\nDRAFTING NOTE (not from source): the final paragraph's \"Sidecarless\""}},"session_id":"62653833-9f48-4f95-9546-6ca47ad80449","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"47a5f080-a7e4-4440-bff0-f03ac80c625d"}
